ly R", "No public general-election polling"], "rationale": "The district's R+9 lean, Foxx's incumbency and overwhelming financial edge point to a comfortable Republican win, and prediction markets price her near 88%. Expert raters mostly call it Safe R, though a few say Likely R, so a Likely R label with a double-digit Republican margin fits the evidence without overcommitting.", "watch": "Any late polling showing Hubbard within single digits, or a major national environment shift toward Democrats, would narrow this.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Virginia Foxx (R) is running."]}, "overview": "North Carolina's 5th District leans firmly Republican, and incumbent Virginia Foxx is seeking another term with a decisive financial advantage. She has raised over $2 million and holds $3.5 million on hand, while Democrat Chuck Hubbard has raised under $800,000 with about $140,000 available. No outside groups are spending meaningfully on Foxx's behalf, and opposition spending has been modest.\n\nRaters overwhelmingly place the race in the Safe or Likely Republican column, and prediction markets give Foxx roughly an 88% chance. With no public general-election polls available, the forecast rests on the district's partisan lean, incumbency, and the money gap, all of which favor the incumbent by a comfortable but not insurmountable margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0624, "margin": -9.74}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0488, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0402, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.028, "margin": -13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0498, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0691, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.063, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0135, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0656, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-